course: dictionary
lesson: 3700
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one is meant. Flatter is a good example. «Bots tend to flatter; praise from a bot that has not seen your work tells you nothing.» Here flatter means to praise someone too much, often not sincerely, just to please them.
explain: The same word can also mean to make someone look better than usual. «That colour flatters you» means the colour makes you look nicer. When Ruby felt flattered, she felt pleased because someone admired her. Look at the clues: who is doing the praising, and how does the person feel?
explain: Flatter can also be an adjective, the comparison of flat. «Water turtles have flatter shells» means less curved and more level. Ask: what word would fit here? Then try your meaning in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Flatter (verb) means to praise someone too much, often not sincerely, to please them or get something.
fact: «Flatter» can also mean to make someone look better than usual, as in «That colour flatters you».
fact: «Be flattered» means feeling pleased because someone admired you.
fact: As an adjective, flatter means more level or smooth, as in «water turtles have flatter shells».
fact: A flatterer is someone who praises others to please them; in an old story, King Canute showed his flattering courtiers that even a king cannot command the tide.
exercise: «Bots tend to flatter; praise from a bot that has not seen your work tells you nothing.» What does flatter mean in this sentence? | *To praise someone too much, often not sincerely | To feel very tired | To climb up a steep hill | To draw bright pictures
exercise: Ruby says, «I'm flattered you asked me.» What does she mean? | Cold, because it is winter | *Pleased, because someone admired her | Hungry and ready to eat | Angry with the person who asked
exercise: «Water turtles have flatter shells.» What does flatter mean in this sentence? | *More level or smooth | Pleasing a king | Praising someone | Hanging down sadly
test: «That colour flatters you.» What does flatters mean here? | It makes you sleepy | *It makes you look better than usual | It makes you feel cold | It makes you run faster
test: In the old story, why did King Canute set his throne by the sea? | To cool down on a hot day | *To show his flattering courtiers that even a king cannot command the tide | To be closer to his ships | To watch the fish swim by
exam: Which sentence uses flatter to mean more level or smooth? | Ruby felt flattered by the invitation | *The flatter road was easier to cycle along | That colour flatters you | Bots tend to flatter people with empty praise
